{"kind":"report","text":"Approved exact head 25f8e453180cb355ab14e4aa22c3a0be8b5023f5 for the complete assigned scope of plans 001, 002 and 004 under request git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b2509b23e82ae7c5aa31535a31f66c595a72df25. Reviewed all 12 artifacts, the complete committed plans, implementation conditions, primary report and novel production/test changes. Estimates did not reduce the acceptance criteria.\n\nArchitecture: the affected Artroom layers are the Git provider and durable cleanup adapters, Room sequencing core, and Durable Object scheduler. In the gitseq architecture model this remains application and storage integration work; it changes neither the signed kernel nor Workroom review authority. Artroom has no docs/reference/architecture.md in this tree; docs/protocol.md remains its public contract. The head repairs existing readiness, cleanup ownership and recovery guarantees without changing public signatures, actor roles, lease authority, sealed repository identity, policy or provider TTLs. The new optional wake port is an internal scheduling capability. The create step and incarnation name are written atomically, and the awaited storage call stays outside synchronous SQL transactions.\n\nSecurity: completeInventory rejects a missing or mismatched total and malformed ID, scope, state or expiry before a listing can establish readiness or settle an inventory. Independent controls confirm withheld workspace grants, no snapshot job credential before readiness, retained deletion/cleanup across restart, recovery with a complete inventory, retention of the recorded lease token and isolation of unrelated canonical tokens. The canonical founding validator keeps its existing requirements through the shared helper.\n\nForeign occupancy proves provenance only. An unknown fork-create or mint step remains in flight, scheduled on a growing capped backoff, even after repeated foreign and absent observations. Answered and owed duties retain their previous settlement behavior. The foreign repository is never swept or changed. A late creation token is revoked by a restarted host, without treating elapsed time or a clean observation as completion of an unknown request.\n\nThe Room now awaits its founding wake before provider dispatch. A rejected pre-effect wake sends no create, records the never-sent outcome and preserves prior legacy debt. Actual workerd controls verify a stored alarm while the first create is outstanding, abort the object, apply that create late and service it through a fresh object's alarm without a founder retry. Earlier stored alarms and concurrent wake requests are preserved; fresh-object recovery schedules older founding debt. Healthy founding, legacy adoption and sealed repository isolation pass. My additional live-host alarm control passes: alarm cleanup waits on the existing founding serial queue while a create is outstanding, then healthy founding completes.\n\nSimplification: the shared inventory validator removes divergent readiness rules; strict count comparison makes the previous separate total type check redundant. The foreign branch uses the existing cleanup finally for backoff rather than another scheduling path. Existing durable state is reused for founding recovery. No extra public states or authority mechanism are needed. I found no material unnecessary mechanism to cut within this scope. The optimistic schedule cache is reset on rejection; its comment is broader than that implementation detail, but this does not weaken the tested conditions.\n\nFresh independent validation at the exact clean head in /tmp/artroom-checker-cc-workspace-v1: root npm run typecheck exit 0; root npm test exit 0, 1,970 passed and 1 skipped (including Git Node 220, Room Node 125 and Room workerd 387); separate Git Worker suite 8 passed; targeted workspaces/snapshots 106 passed; Room wrangler deploy --dry-run with wrangler.spike.jsonc exit 0; scope and whitespace checks pass. Dependencies were copied from the builder's installed workspace; I do not claim an independent npm ci.\n\nIn a separate diagnostic clone, all 26 reported guard mutations independently produced named runtime test failures, with no import or transform failures. Two additional mutants removing Core-to-Workspaces and Room-to-Core wake wiring fail the real DO persisted-alarm and failed-wake controls. My SQLite interruption control passes on the head and fails when the new incarnation transaction is removed: earlier legacy debt survives, the partial new step rolls back, no wake or provider call is sent, and a healthy retry completes. Thus 29 independently exercised mutations were rejected. Production files were restored after every diagnostic; the reviewed checkout stayed clean.\n\nEvidence limits: one exploratory alarm test initially waited for alarm completion while holding the founding serial queue and timed out; that harness ordering was corrected before drawing a conclusion. A synthetic constructor fault thrown before storage.setAlarm leaves no alarm, but is not evidence of an equivalent production storage-write failure. Cloudflare documents that failed storage writes reset the object and discard outgoing messages, and setAlarm uses the same storage options (https://developers.cloudflare.com/durable-objects/api/sqlite-storage-api/). I withdraw that exploratory production finding. No claim here depends on an unawaited storage call bypassing output gates.\n\nThe 601-file head preserves 589 paths byte-for-byte from main a319360aed3475e6c5b1534fd37f78e5790a47a8, modifies the eight scoped existing paths and adds the four assigned plan/report files. No dependency, lockfile or unrelated source change. This review credits those unchanged paths from main; it does not approve plan 003, which still has changes requested, or the separate snapshot/founded-recovery/jobs-validator request git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c9cd4cd859e9f715a743a674845e1c7e0cc4b994. The canonical mint ownership and cleanup visibility handoffs also remain separate. Nothing was deployed, no live provider deletion, inference or credential creation was performed. Approval is for this exact artifact set; incorporation still needs its normal sealed gitseq receipt.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:dc3172ef28d923af7c45f0d0d535fdc9d5d4f316","binding":"assigned","head":"25f8e453180cb355ab14e4aa22c3a0be8b5023f5","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a61f6642709c6c4d06ba3c3823a8dc0120d1751a\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6fc4fee1f415754931a60f29d3bc7cd29dfba78b\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:a61f6642709c6c4d06ba3c3823a8dc0120d1751a","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}